# Vantrock Intelligence — environment configuration
#
# The local-first MVP runs with NO configuration at all. Every variable below
# has a safe default. Copy to .env.local only if you want to override.
#
# NEVER put a real secret in this file. It is committed.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Persistence backend
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# "indexeddb" — browser-local storage (default, zero configuration)
# "supabase"  — Postgres/PostGIS backend. Requires the Supabase block below
#               AND the migration in supabase/migrations/ to have been run.
#               See docs/MANUAL_ACTIONS.md.
NEXT_PUBLIC_PERSISTENCE_DRIVER=indexeddb

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Basemap
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# "osm-dev" — OpenStreetMap raster tiles. Free, no API key. DEVELOPMENT ONLY:
#             the OSMF tile usage policy does not permit production apps.
# "blank"   — no network at all. Fully offline; local reference layers only.
NEXT_PUBLIC_BASEMAP=osm-dev

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase — required only when NEXT_PUBLIC_PERSISTENCE_DRIVER=supabase
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Project URL and anon/public key from Supabase Dashboard -> Project Settings
# -> API. The anon key is safe in the browser — it is constrained by the RLS
# policies in supabase/migrations/0001_init.sql, never by keeping it secret.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
#
# Service/secret key — SERVER-ONLY. Never prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_, never
# import under app/ in a client component. Not read by any code yet (no
# privileged server-side Supabase operation exists in this MVP); reserved for
# when one is added.
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Demo access gate — server-side password, HTTP-only session cookie
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SERVER-ONLY. Unset = no login gate (local dev convenience). Set this in any
# deployed environment. See docs/MANUAL_ACTIONS.md and docs/SECURITY.md.
# DEMO_ACCESS_PASSWORD=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OpenRouter (server-side AI) — Underwrite / Research modes
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SERVER-ONLY — never prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_. AI_PROVIDER=openrouter with a
# valid key/model enables the real model; anything else (unset, "demo", or a
# missing/invalid key) falls back to the deterministic demo provider — the
# app never requires this to run. See docs/AI_ARCHITECTURE.md.
# AI_PROVIDER=demo
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=
# OPENROUTER_MAX_TOKENS=900
# OPENROUTER_TEMPERATURE=0.2
